{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "Swap object in video from a reference image (SAM 3.1 + Wan2.2 Fun VACE, masked paste-back)",
    "description": "Core nodes + h3-relay LabsH3PrepareVideo + cj_h3_tools. Same masking and paste-back as video_object_remove, plus a reference image of the replacement. LoadVideo -> LabsH3PrepareVideo (24 fps, ~0.5 MP on the 32-px grid, first 3 s = 73 frames, 4n+1 for VACE) -> SAM 3.1 text-prompted video tracking (node 31 = what to replace; Smart select clicks can replace this branch) -> SAM3_TrackToMask -> GrowMask (wider than removal so a differently shaped object fits) -> CJMaskTemporal (max) -> WanVaceToVideo: control video = original frames with the masked area neutral grey, control_masks = the mask (1 = regenerate), reference_image = the replacement object (LoadImage -> BiRefNet RemoveBackground -> ImageCropToMask on white -> ResizeAndPadImage white to the video size, VACE's subject-reference convention; the builder can skip the cut-out) -> two-stage Wan2.2 Fun VACE sampling (balanced: hi w/o LoRA 8 steps cfg 3.5 0-4, lo + lightx2v cfg 1; fast: LoRA both, 4 steps cfg 1) -> TrimVideoLatent drops the reference latent -> trim to the real frame count -> CJPasteBackSave: generated pixels only inside the mask, the source everywhere else at source resolution, source audio copied. A second CJMaskTemporal (node 38, max, radius 4 = the worst distance between a frame and the frame WanVaceToVideo samples for its latent's mask) feeds control_masks and the paste-back's expanded_mask: VACE keeps one frame's mask per 4-frame latent, so a fast limb greyed in a frame the sample missed was copied as grey (smear); with the wider latent mask every greyed pixel is regenerated."
  },
